coder v0.0.0-devel

USAGE:
  coder exp api [flags] <path>

  Make an authenticated HTTP request to the Coder API and print the response.

  The path is relative to /api/v2/ unless it starts with a slash. Fields are
  sent as query parameters for GET and HEAD requests and as a JSON object
  otherwise. The method defaults to GET, or POST when fields or --input are
  provided, so use -X GET to send fields as query parameters.
  
    - Get the authenticated user:
  
       $ coder exp api users/me
  
    - List workspaces with a query parameter:
  
       $ coder exp api -X GET workspaces -f q=owner:me
  
    - Send a JSON body from stdin:
  
       $ echo '{"name":"new-name"}' | coder exp api -X PATCH workspaces/<id>
  --input -

OPTIONS:
  -f, --field string-array
          Add a string parameter in key=value format. Can be specified multiple
          times.

  -i, --include bool
          Print the response status line and headers before the body.

      --input string
          The file to use as the request body, or - to read from stdin.

  -X, --method string
          The HTTP method for the request.

  -H, --request-header string-array
          Add a request header in key:value format. Can be specified multiple
          times.

———
Run `coder --help` for a list of global options.
